  "caption": "Quinn discovered rucking and packed every tin in the pantry. Day one ended hunched over. Plan B, ankle weights, wasn't better.\n\nWalking with a weighted backpack can add strength, bone loading and cardio at walking-level impact. Ankle or hand weights aren't the same, as they change how you walk and can irritate joints.\n\nWhat can help: starting around 5–10% of body weight (often 4–6 kg), 30–40 minutes once or twice a week on flat routes, changing one thing at a time (time, then hills, then weight), using both straps and the hip belt, a slightly shorter stride and supportive shoes.\n\nCheck with a health professional first if you're mid-rehab or have osteoporosis, balance problems or a heart condition.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
